"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative aimed at revolutionizing the company's approach to the field. It was introduced by Alex with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000, led by Sarah Tan. The project has since seen several developments: the budget was increased to $550,000 to cover unforeseen expenses and real-time analytics integration; strategic partnerships with TechInnovate for AI research were established; and the team expanded to include Mike Chen and Lisa Ray for machine learning and cloud computing expertise. A call for ideas was issued to R&D to leverage AI for data visualization, with proposals due by July 20th. The project reached its first major milestone ahead of schedule with a successfully tested secure file sharing prototype, and user interface enhancements are planned for October. Additionally, a training budget of $15,000 was approved for the coding team and project managers. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is currently being sought from stakeholders by the end of November."
